    {
        "content": "<p>So I have started a refactor, see <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42048\">#42048</a>, that weakens the hypotheses of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Ideal.absNorm#doc\">docs#Ideal.absNorm</a>. At the moment, the API requires the ring to be a Dedekind domain that is also a free ℤ-module (and furthermore finite in most lemmas). The refactor replaces that with any infinite Dedekind domain with finite quotients.</p>\n<p>A few lemmas genuinely rely on a ℤ-basis and stay unchanged. Since a free finite ℤ-module satisfies all the new hypotheses, nothing downstream needs to change. Quite a few results further downstream can probably be generalized now, that part is still WIP.</p>\n<p>The PR is meant to be split into smaller pieces before it goes into Mathlib (assuming people agree this is a sensible refactor), so consider it more as a proof of concept at this stage.</p>",
        "id": 612481448,
        "sender_full_name": "Xavier Roblot",
        "timestamp": 1784859229
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh yikes, we definitely want this to work for rings like <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">F</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{F}_p[T]</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">F</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>, this sounds like a great idea to me!</p>",
        "id": 612518846,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1784879988
    },
